[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: A large projected image of city buildings with red lighting in a living room setup.
AUDIO: 'So, the internet has been absolutely flooded with reviews of the XJimmy Titan or Max, but sadly their more affordable Pro model hasn\'t received the same type of exposure. In today\'s video, if you\'re looking to save a little bit of money compared to what you\'d spend on the Max, I\'ll be going over the best features of'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the Titan Pro, as well as real life examples of performance in a variety of different environments. So, without further ado, let\'s begin. Now, as far as the aesthetics, they went'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with this minimal, no thrills, what I\'m calling an industrial design. And obviously, personal preference on looks, but I\'m always a big fan of this style. However, I do wish at some point they would make this available in white to better fit in with my gaming room. And'

[00:53] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: Gameplay footage displayed on a large screen in a dimly lit room, showcasing the projector's gaming capabilities.
AUDIO: 'as far as some of the main selling points, this offers a crazy high 6,000 ISO lumens. It has a dynamic iris, which I\'ll get into later, 8000 to1 native contrast. It supports Dolby Vision, HDR10 Plus, IMAX, Filmmaker mode, and'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it\'s extremely versatile from an installation standpoint thanks to its optical zoom and horizontal and vertical lens shift. And for gaming, it does 4K at 60 Hz, 1080p at 240, and it has 1 millisecond of input lag.'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'On the back is where you\'ll find all your hookups with your DC in optical, two USB ports, three HDMI inputs, your audio, LAN, and power. Now, I\'ll be testing things out on my 120in ALR'

[01:32] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A vibrant animated landscape projected onto a large screen in a living room, demonstrating color reproduction.
AUDIO: 'screen in my basement, my cheap 150inch regular white screen in my living room, my 120in ALR screen in my gaming room, my 120in ALR screen in my bedroom, as well as a plain white wall. All right, so the first thing I want to call out'

[01:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'right away is that the hype is actually real. From a performance standpoint to date, this produces the best looking picture I\'ve yet to see from a standard or US projector that I\'ve tested out. Now, I\'ve watched a lot of reviews from different people and everyone said how'

[01:58] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A scene of a forest projected onto a screen, with a small "JK" logo in the bottom right corner.
AUDIO: 'they were blown away with the contrast that XJimmy was able to achieve. And now I can officially say I understand what they\'re talking about because it really is incredible how good it looks in person. The colors are bright and vibrant, the blacks are dark, and thanks to their dynamic iris, it\'s able to'

[02:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'adjust the contrast in real time to give you the best looking image no matter what the scene. And here\'s a good example of this in action. I\'ll pause it right here at a new scene and notice how the image looks. I\'ll unpause it and you can see how the picture slightly'

[02:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'darkens. and I\'ll replay it again in case you missed it. But this is what having a dynamic iris means where it\'ll automatically adjust the brightness and contrast levels in real time to give you the best results. However, if you don\'t want to have this feature enabled, you'

[02:36] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A vibrant, colorful image projected onto a screen, with on-screen controls for "Dynamic" and iris settings (f/2.0 to f/7.0).
AUDIO: 'have five different iris levels you can choose between depending on your liking. And here, as you can see in iris settings, it\'s currently set to dynamic. I\'ll go through the five different levels you can manually set it to. And every time you go higher, the iris is clamping down further to let less light'

[02:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'escape. Now, in a completely dark room like this and on a ALR screen, 7 is the only one I probably wouldn\'t use, but there is a use case for this darkest option that I\'ll go over a little later on. Now, because of how bright this'

[03:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'projector gets with its 6,000 isol, this means you can absolutely use it in ambient lighting conditions, but this is where I would for sure recommend an ALR screen. And halfway through filming, I received my 130in ALR flooring screen from Nothing Projector. And you can see'

[03:14] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A wide shot of a living room with a large projected image of a scenic bay, demonstrating ambient light performance.
AUDIO: 'how even with the window directly to the left of the image, the picture looks incredibly sharp. And when I roll down my blinds, it gets even better. And this is still with an incredible amount of ambient light coming in from other parts of the house. And fun fact about this'

[03:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'screen is it\'s actually meant for US projectors because I have a couple videos coming up that I\'ll be needing it for. And yes, while the image and picture looks incredible, I\'m curious if anyone can pick up on something that\'s a dead giveaway that I\'m using the wrong type of projector with the screen.'

[03:39] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: An animated scene with a large mechanical castle in a mountainous landscape projected onto a screen.
AUDIO: 'I\'ll pause it here. And if you saw this multicolored bar on the screen, then you'

[03:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are correct. This is something that will almost always show up if you\'re using a standard throw projector on an ALR screen designed for an ultrash short throw device. All right, so this one might be a little controversial, but I wanted to get other people\'s opinion.'

[04:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Here, I\'ll first be playing some footage in the standard mode format where the colors are bright, vibrant, and saturated. And in my opinion, I think it looks great. Now, most of the high-end projectors have what\'s called filmmaker mode, and I\'m wondering if I\'m the only'

[04:15] [scene:comparison]
VISUAL: Side-by-side comparison of "standard" and "filmmaker" modes displaying the same scene, highlighting color differences.
AUDIO: 'one that personally never turns this on. I\'ll go ahead and play some footage side by side, but I am curious to know if I\'m alone in this or if there are others who feel the same way. So, this next feature is for anyone out'

[04:48] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: Bright, colorful animated scene projected onto a plain white wall in a well-lit room, demonstrating performance without a dedicated screen.
AUDIO: 'there with kids. Me personally, I have six of them. And one of the coolest features of this projector is instead of turning the screen completely off when it detects a person, it\'s somehow able to only dim the area around your head. So, for example, if you\'re watching'

[05:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sports, you might not completely miss the big play when one of your kids walk in front. Now, I was super curious to see how this would perform on what\'s probably an absolute worst case scenario with white walls, white carpet, and a white ceiling. And going back to the'

[05:13] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A scene from Avatar: The Way of Water projected onto a white wall, showcasing detail and color in a bright room.
AUDIO: 'adjustable iris in this type of environment, I\'ll go through the five stops. And this is where the last one, which was too dark on my ALR screen, actually blew me away with how good it looked on the wall. I\'ll play some more footage here, but I was shocked at these'

[05:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'results. So, if you don\'t want to get an ALR screen or you\'re planning to save up for one, just know that projecting straight onto your wall is certainly an option. &gt;&gt; No good. What? &gt;&gt; Fly.'

[05:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For audio, it has two 12 watt Harmon'

[06:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Cardon speakers. And for a projector, it sounds about as good as you could expect. It\'ll never replace a good surround sound setup, but if you\'re like me who will use this all over the house, it\'s certainly passable. &gt;&gt; So, this is my gaming room setup that I'

[06:25] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: Racing game footage displayed on a large screen, showing in-game UI elements and car movement.
AUDIO: 'built from scratch. And in case you didn\'t see that video, I\'ll leave a link to it in the description. But against the back wall, I have a 120in ALR screen. And once you\'ve experienced gaming on something this size, it\'s very hard to go back to a normal size'

[06:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'monitor. Now, like I mentioned earlier, this does 4K at 60 Hz and 1080p at up to 240. But if the main reason for getting a projector is for gaming, I\'ll leave a link to XJimmy\'s brand new ultra short throw projector that they just announced'

[06:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that will do 4K at 120 Hz among other things. So make sure to check that out if you\'re interested. Don\'t make me go over there.'

[07:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Next, I\'ll go back up to my living room.'

[07:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And this is a very inexpensive 150in screen. It\'s just a simple white plastic material with no special qualities. I\'ll go back and forth between a couple different angles so you can see how good the picture looks without having to spend a ton of money on a type screen if you don\'t want to.'

[07:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And as far as noise levels, this is one'

[08:06] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A smartphone displaying a decibel meter app, showing a reading of 37.2 dB, placed near the projector to measure noise levels.
AUDIO: 'of the quietest projectors I\'ve ever tested. When 2 ft away, I\'m getting about 33 dB, which is just above a whisper. And when I go a couple inches away from the fans in the back, it\'s only jumping up to 35 on the right side and around 36 on the left. And even with'

[08:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the sound muted, you can hardly pick up on any noise. So, if this is something that\'s important to you, you\'ll definitely be happy. And of course, I had to test this out on my DIY ambulite setup, and it looked absolutely incredible. I\'ll leave a link'

[08:30] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A wide shot of a home theater setup with a large projected image of a sky scene, enhanced by ambient lighting strips.
AUDIO: 'to a video walkthrough I did on this setup, but in a nutshell, I\'m using a couple Gladopto Elite WLED controllers, some individually addressable SK6812 LEDs, a bunch of Matada U108 spotless diffuser channels, and a brand new Scene'

[08:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and Glow app to make it all come together. Now, I know 3D is pretty much pointless'

[09:00] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Overhead shot of the XGIMI Titan Noir Pro projector next to an Nvidia Shield, showcasing its compact design.
AUDIO: 'trying to film, but this is another area that the Titan excels in. The image remains bright and sharp when 3D is turned on and viewing with 3D glasses. And since I\'m starting to get a pretty nice collection of 3D movies, having this capability, at least for me, is a'

[09:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'must for any projector that I would buy. So, in a world where most projectors have a built-in OS, like Android TV, the XJimmy Titan lineup does not. This means you have to use an HDMI device as your'

[09:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'input, such as an Nvidia Shield, something like the Digi Box, a Fire Stick, Apple TV, a Roku, PlayStation, Nintendo, or any of the other options out there. And this isn\'t a huge deal if you always have this in one place, but'

[09:38] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: Dark, detailed sci-fi scene projected onto a screen in a very dark room, highlighting contrast.
AUDIO: 'for me that does a lot of testing in different areas, it would be nice not to have to plug in anything else. So, that about does it for this one, but I think the best way to summarize this projector is that unless you\'re holding out for a 4K 120 Hz unit, I don\'t think there\'s any way you could possibly regret buying'

[09:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the XJimmy Titan Pro. The brightness and contrast are what I would consider to be bestin-class. And in the two weeks I\'ve been testing this out, I can confidently say that XJimmy isn\'t holding back any punches, and they\'re in a great position'

[10:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to be leaders in the space for years to come. I\'ll leave you with some more of my favorite examples. But thank you all so much for watching, and as always, I hope you have a blessed day. Nat.'

